        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "Summary: CLINICAL ASSESSMENT FOR 18-64 YEARS (ADULT) PATIENT:\nBased on reported symptoms (Fever, Headache), the primary suspected condition is **COVID-19 (Coronavirus)** with a calculated **20.0% clinical match**.\nDifferential considerations include: Acute Bronchitis (17.9%), Typhoid Fever (14.3%).\n\nHome Care: \u2022 Isolate in a well-ventilated room to prevent transmission.\n\u2022 Monitor SpO2 with a pulse oximeter every 4-6 hours.\n\u2022 Warm saline gargles and steam inhalation for throat relief.\n\u2022 Generous hydration and balanced, protein-rich nutrition.\n\nMedical Attention: \u26a0\ufe0f URGENCY LEVEL: MILD\nWatch for the following Warning Signs:\n\u2022 Oxygen saturation (SpO2) < 94%\n\u2022 Persistent chest pressure\n\u2022 Confusion\n\u2022 Bluish lips/face\n\nClinical Recommendation: Seek emergency care if SpO2 drops below 94% or severe breathing difficulty occurs.\n\nPossible Causes: Primary Pathophysiology: A contagious respiratory infection caused by SARS-CoV-2, ranging from mild cold-like symptoms to viral pneumonia.\n\nRecommended Tests / Confirmation: Consult a physician for formal clinical verification and diagnostic confirmation.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-17T14:03:40.207618"
        }
